-- title:
--   Commute GHalf Sandwich Move Back Chain Family Zero Eq Second Slice Lift Move Family
-- statement:
--   **The zero-index move-back family is the lifted move-family endpoint.**
--
--   Let `params` have a field model, let `family` be an indexed polynomial family, let `r` be a natural number, let `q` be a move-chain question in `MoveQ(params,r+1)`, and let `ogs` be a matching outcome in `MoveO(params,r+1)`. The outcome at index zero of the move-back chain is exactly the second-slice lift of the length-`r` move family:
--
--   $$
--   \begin{aligned}
--   &\bigl(\operatorname{commuteGHalfSandwich\_moveBackChainFamily}(\mathrm{params},\mathrm{family},r,0)(q)\bigr).\operatorname{outcome}(ogs)\\
--   &=\bigl(\operatorname{commuteGHalfSandwich\_secondSliceLiftFamily}(\mathrm{params},\mathrm{family},r,
--   \operatorname{commuteGHalfSandwich\_moveFamily}(\mathrm{params},\mathrm{family},r))(q)\bigr).\operatorname{outcome}(ogs).
--   \end{aligned}
--   $$
--
--   The equality is pointwise in both questions and outcomes. It identifies the first reverse-chain node with the lifted forward move endpoint, allowing the corresponding qSDD edge to be reused in the flat chain.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.commuteGHalfSandwich_moveBackChainFamily_zero_eq_secondSliceLift_moveFamily`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
